# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a `git checkout`
# (including any branch switch) rewrites tracked files with CRLF. That is
# harmless for most of them, but it silently breaks every executable script
# that starts with a shebang: vitest's transform mis-parses `#!/usr/bin/env
# node\r\n` and reports "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" pointing at
# a comment several lines away, so the failure looks like a code defect in a
# file that is actually fine. Observed on scripts/export-capability-schemas.js
# and eval/run.js after a branch switch, with node itself importing both
# without complaint.
#
# The repository content has always been LF (git normalises on commit), and
# the server runs on Linux, so this only ever affected local Windows checkouts
# — but a test suite that fails for reasons invisible in the diff is worse
# than one that fails honestly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.msi binary
